			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"text": "Alarm Bell Signaled\n\nAmygdala (oldest evolutionary \npart of our brains, key \nnoticing danger and the fear \nresponse, key to survival) \nsounds alarm bells.",
			"rawText": "Alarm Bell Signaled\n\nAmygdala (oldest evolutionary part of our brains, key noticing danger and the fear response, key to survival) sounds alarm bells.",
			"baseline": 168,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "jJmInf-nf5g97bSYK3toK",
			"originalText": "Alarm Bell Signaled\n\nAmygdala (oldest evolutionary part of our brains, key noticing danger and the fear response, key to survival) sounds alarm bells."
		},
