		{
			"type": "text",
			"version": 899,
			"versionNonce": 1048003783,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"id": "2NFVRCke",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"x": 408.7674919262265,
			"y": 473.5422139753373,
			"strokeColor": "#c92a2a",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"width": 346,
			"height": 200,
			"seed": 624929607,
			"groupIds": [],
			"roundness": null,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1675185097805,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"text": "Prefrontal cortex inhibited by \nnorepinephrine, so unable to think \nrationally -\nThe negativity bias of amygdala \ndumps more and more negative \nmemories into the hippocampus, \ncolouring our view of the world as \nfearful, unpleasant. ",
			"rawText": "Prefrontal cortex inhibited by norepinephrine, so unable to think rationally -\nThe negativity bias of amygdala dumps more and more negative memories into the hippocampus, colouring our view of the world as fearful, unpleasant. ",
			"baseline": 193,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "ZORb2cHFeEnvs1jOyBwxU",
			"originalText": "Prefrontal cortex inhibited by norepinephrine, so unable to think rationally -\nThe negativity bias of amygdala dumps more and more negative memories into the hippocampus, colouring our view of the world as fearful, unpleasant. "
		},
